    Register apps.install plug-ins and rotate on iOS 27 with icli 0.7.14
    
    vphoned's apps.install registered an app's PlugIns/*.appex at their
    paths in the temporary copy of the IPA, so LaunchServices kept no
    record of them, and on iOS 27 it dropped them altogether: nothing could
    find or launch an installed app's extensions. A packet tunnel provider
    failed with NEAgentErrorDomain Code=2 and no process (#546). icli 0.7.12
    and 0.7.13 register them at their installed paths on both, and the
    result reports plugins and unregistered_plugins.
    
    SpringBoard on iOS 27 refuses the accessibility server's rotate and
    orientation-lock requests from a client without
    com.apple.accessibility.physicalinteraction.client, so display.rotation
    and display.rotation_lock left the interface where it was. vphoned
    carries that entitlement now, as icli 0.7.14 does.
    
    Checked on an iOS 27 RootHide guest through vphoned: an IPA with a
    packet tunnel extension installed by apps.install lists its plug-in,
    and the tunnel's provider launches and connects; rotation to 90, 270
    and 0 and the orientation lock apply.
    
